ding documents, updating systems, chasing information and resolving exceptions instead of managing claims.</p></article><article class="challenge"><div aria-hidden="true" class="ico"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg></div><h3>Compliance and vendors run outside the claim record</h3><p>Reporting requirements apply from underwriting to claim closure, and the hard part is often the failed submission. Dozens of vendors work without common data on referrals, performance and cost.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="band b "><div class="container-fluid px-4"><div class="split-head"><h2 class="gw-section-title">How Mahathi Helps</h2><div class="lead-in"><strong>How Mahathi helps carriers, employers and TPAs respond.</strong>Technology programs focus on systems and outsourcing programs focus on people. Workers&#x27; compensation needs both working together, so Mahathi delivers them as one engagement.</div></div><div class="solutions-grid" style="margin-bottom:56px"><article class="solution"><div class="sol-num">01</div><h3>One claims platform for operations that ran apart.</h3><p class="sol-body">A carrier needed to bring a significant assigned-risk workers&#x27; compensation book, written across multiple states, into its voluntary operation. Mahathi led configuration, integration, claims data migration and operational enablement on a common Guidewire ClaimCenter foundation.</p><div class="sol-proof"><span class="sol-proof-num">1</span><span class="sol-proof-text">claims platform for operations that were previously separate</span></div></article><article class="solution"><div class="sol-num">02</div><h3>Earlier sight of emerging claim risk.</h3><p 